<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00007273> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00007273> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-27"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Positive regulation of gluconeogenesis by glucagon/GCGR (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                   "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "2026-10-13: upstream units (glucagon, GCGR, GNAS, ADCY6, PKA) moved from part_of GO:0007189 to part_of GO:0045722 'positive regulation of gluconeogenesis' (curator choice; one BP per activity, matching CRTC2/CREB1). Evidence (abstracts only): glucagon ISS MGI:95674 (PMID:24051374 MGI IDA; PMID:20592160 glucagon loss reduces hepatic glucose production). GCGR IDA PMID:35767325 (glucagon/GCGR induces PCK1 in Huh-7-Lunet cells with epitope-tagged GCGR, and PCK1/PGC1a/G6PC in primary hepatocytes via endogenous GCGR; receptor and hepatocyte species not stated in abstract - check full text) + ISS MGI:99572 (PMID:12552113 Gcgr-/- lower blood glucose). GNAS ISS MGI:95777 (PMID:16239968 liver-specific Gsa KO: low hepatic gluconeogenic enzyme expression when fed; fasting glucose normal). ADCY6 ISS MGI:87917 (PMID:31918924, INDIRECT: Purb raises Adcy6 transcription and glucagon-driven glucose production; no direct Adcy6 loss-of-function). PKA ISS MGI:97592 (PMID:23292513 MGI IDA: metformin lowers cAMP/PKA and blocks glucagon-dependent glucose output in mouse hepatocytes; pharmacological)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Built by claude4go with curator 2026-10-13 as the glucagon counterpart of gomodel:6ab067da00006950 (OXM/GCGR). Same hepatocyte cascade (GCGR -> Gs -> ADCY6 -> cAMP -> PKA -> CREB1/CRTC2 -> PCK1, G6PC1); only the ligand unit differs. Mostly abstract-level evidence; full texts not read."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "GNAS->ADCY6: human ADCY6 activated by Galpha-s in vitro (PMID:17110384, abstract; Gs species not stated) -> IC. ADCY6 choice for hepatocyte: mouse glucagon/ADCY6/cAMP/PKA/CREB pathway in hepatocytes (PMID:31918924)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Glucagon->GCGR: glucagon peptide UniProtKB:P01275-PRO_0000011256 (aa 53-81). IDA PMID:9287038 (human GCGR expressed in CHO cells; glucagon binding, cAMP accumulation and Ca2+ mobilization; abstract). Glucagon species not stated in the abstract, but the peptide is identical in human, rat and mouse. GCGR part_of hepatocyte now cites PMID:31918924 (mouse glucagon/GCGR/PKA pathway in hepatocytes) instead of the OXM paper used in the OXM model."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "PKA->CREB1 Ser133: PMID:2573431 (rat PC12) -> ISS RGD. CRTC2: mouse TORC2 regulates fasting gluconeogenic CREB transcription (PMID:16148943) -> ISS MGI. CREB1->PCK1/G6PC1: mouse CREB mutants reduce gluconeogenic gene expression (PMID:11557984) -> ISS MGI; note that in that study CREB acts largely via PGC-1 (not modelled). Not modelled: PKA-SIK2 control of CRTC2, CBP/p300, PGC-1alpha."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

